The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a> 2 could retain the original model's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a> despite gaining a second rear camera, according to observations about recently shared dummy models.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/09/Living-With-the-iPhone-Air-Thumb-3.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1021596" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://weibo.com/3108827753/5367676026490067">post on Weibo</a>, the blogger known as "Experience More" highlighted the apparently unchanged display cutout in images of the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; 2 and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a> dummy models <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/20/iphone-air-2-and-iphone-18-dummy-models/">shared by Sonny Dickson</a> last week. The user questioned why the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; 2 mockup appears to lack the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/18/iphone-18-pro-teardown/">smaller Dynamic Island</a> introduced on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> models.<br/>
<br/>
Experience More suggested that the explanation could lie in the device's internal layout, which they have previously shared details about. The &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj;'s revised internal design places the front-facing camera toward the right of the &zwnj;Dynamic Island&zwnj;, but adding an Ultra Wide rear camera to the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; 2 could leave insufficient room for a similar configuration.<br/>
<br/>
The suggestion has some support in earlier rumors about Apple's efforts to fit another camera into the thin device. In January, the leaker known as "Instant Digital" claimed that Apple had requested an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/26/apple-developing-thinner-face-id-iphone-air-2/">ultra-thin Face ID component</a> from suppliers specifically to create space for an Ultra Wide camera alongside the existing main camera.<br/>
<br/>
The original &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/20/ifixit-iphone-air-teardown/">concentrates multiple components</a> in its raised camera plateau to leave more room for the battery. Accommodating another rear camera therefore requires changes to an already tightly packed area. <br/>
<br/>
